<Base title="Federica Iengo | Data Analytics & AI Search" description="Federica Iengo works across Data Analytics, AI Search, GEO, AEO and SEO, turning fragmented information into measurable, useful insight.">
<section class="hero">
<p class="eyebrow">Data Analytics · AI Search · GEO · AEO · SEO</p>
<h1>I make complex information easier to understand, measure and use.</h1>
<p class="lead">My work sits between data analysis and AI search. I use SQL and Python to investigate data, and I study how search and generative systems retrieve, interpret, cite and recommend information.</p>
<div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="/projects">Explore projects</a><a class="button" href="/about">About me</a></div>
</section>

<section class="proof">
<p class="eyebrow">Current focus</p>
<div class="grid">
<article class="card"><h3>Measure</h3><p>Build reproducible datasets and metrics for AI visibility, citations, retrieval and competitive analysis.</p></article>
<article class="card"><h3>Diagnose</h3><p>Find content, entity, evidence and data-quality gaps instead of reducing a problem to a single score.</p></article>
<article class="card"><h3>Improve</h3><p>Turn findings into testable changes, then keep proposed interventions separate from measured outcomes.</p></article>
</div>
</section>

<section>
<div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Selected work</p><h2>Projects built around evidence</h2></div><a href="/projects">View all projects →</a></div>
<div class="grid featured">
<a class="card project-card" href="/projects/seo-aeo-geo-optimization"><span class="project-type">AI Search · Case study</span><h3>SEO/AEO/GEO Optimization</h3><p>An independent Notion case study moving from public baseline and query fan-out to diagnosis, proposed optimization and controlled measurement design.</p><span class="project-link">Read case study →</span></a>
<a class="card project-card" href="/projects/ai-search-competitive-intelligence"><span class="project-type">AI Search · Competitive intelligence</span><h3>AI Search Competitive Intelligence</h3><p>A controlled benchmark across Notion, Asana, ClickUp and monday.com using 35 frozen prompts, first-party evidence and auditable scoring rules.</p><span class="project-link">Explore benchmark →</span></a>
<article class="card project-card"><span class="project-type">Data · Snowflake · dbt</span><h3>E-Commerce Revenue & Operations Analytics</h3><p>Nine related datasets audited with Python, modelled through Snowflake and dbt, then investigated for lifecycle anomalies and financial reconciliation.</p></article>
<article class="card project-card"><span class="project-type">Data · PostgreSQL · Tableau</span><h3>Insurance Claims Analytics</h3><p>Analysis of financial exposure, claim severity, portfolio concentration and data quality with an executive reporting layer.</p></article>
</div>
</section>

<section class="principle">
<p class="eyebrow">Working principle</p>
<h2>Evidence first. Claims second.</h2>
<p>I keep observed facts, analysis, proposed changes and measured outcomes separate. That matters in data work, and it matters just as much when evaluating visibility in AI-generated answers.</p>
</section>
</Base>

